{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>For Mine is every firstborn.</b> Previously the service was performed by the firstborn." "<b>On the day I struck every firstborn in the land of Egypt, I consecrated to Me every firstborn in Israel.</b> Indeed, in the plague of the firstborn, the firstborn were liable to be punished for the sin of the generation, because they were the most distinguished among them, and because they were not liable to be spared from a national calamity, as in the matter of ״lest you be swept away in the iniquity of the city״ (Genesis 19:15). And I delivered them in that I consecrated them to Me, so that they would be forbidden to engage in lay labor, like all consecrated things, which are forbidden for shearing and labor. And in order that they might be permitted in this respect, I required of them redemption, like all consecrated things that pass to ordinary use, as it says (Exodus 34:20): ״All the firstborn of your sons you shall redeem.״ And it was not on account of this redemption that they were exempt from the service. But now that they have sinned, I have rejected them, and I have taken the Levites in their stead as redemption. <b>And the Levites shall be Mine</b> for the service." "<b>From man to beast, they shall be Mine.</b> From here onward, the man for redemption and the beast for sacrifice." "<b>I am YHWH.</b> I did not change when I rejected the firstborn, for this change occurred not from My side but from theirs, because they sinned. And likewise when I desired that the Levites redeem the firstborn in this generation but not so henceforth — for indeed in this generation they are fit for this, but not so henceforth."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:00.434565283Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}